//- This talk's own mixins. Lemon's shared ones are in _mixins.pug.

//- An eyedropper reading off one pixel of a photo, like Figma's or Photoshop's: a ring on the spot, a hairline out to a chip with the sampled swatch and its hex. x and y are the ring's centre in cqw and cqh of the canvas, and hex is the pixel's real colour, sampled from the image file. scss/talk/_eyedropper.scss draws it.
mixin eyedropper(x, y, hex)
  .eyedropper(style=`--x: ${x}; --y: ${y}; --sample: ${hex};`)&attributes(attributes)
    span.chip
      span.swatch
      code= hex
    span.lead
    span.ring
